<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.kipi.launchd-health -- the launchd silent-death watchdog.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (ASK-1345, sp-173ead80). The label was loaded on the
  founder's machine on 2026-06-30 from a hand-written plist and NOTHING in the
  repo carried a template for it: `git log --all --diff-filter=A` over 3140
  commits returns nothing for this basename, and no copy sat in any worktree.
  A machine rebuild lost the fleet's own watchdog silently, and the repaired
  enumerator could not install it because there was nothing to enumerate.

  Transcribed from the live ~/Library/LaunchAgents copy, not invented: same
  interpreter, same script, same two fire times, same log paths. The hardcoded
  home in that copy is the reason this is a template rather than a checked-in
  plist -- install-plist.sh substitutes __KIPI_REPO__, __HOME__ and __USER__, so
  the same file works on a machine that is not this one.

  kipi-scope: skeleton-only
  (install-plist.sh --all reads that marker and skips this template anywhere but
  the skeleton.) SKELETON ONLY because this label is a per-machine singleton: it
  enumerates ~/Library/LaunchAgents for every watched prefix and reports on all
  of them at once. launchd-health-check.py propagates to instances via
  kipi update, so without this marker `--all` from any of 23 instance checkouts
  would rebind the one watchdog label to that instance -- the same label
  collision the marker was added for on com.kipi.lessons-daily.

  THE TWO FIRE TIMES ARE TRANSCRIBED, NOT ENDORSED. sp-41409ffe is open against
  them: launchd-health-check.py's FAIL_PING_TTL_SECONDS is 6h while these are 12h
  apart, so the TTL leg of problems_to_ping can never suppress and a chronically
  failing job alerts on every run. Committing the live schedule is deliberate --
  this template's job is to make the loaded job reproducible, and changing its
  cadence in the same breath would ship an untested behaviour change to a
  machine-wide watchdog. Whoever fixes sp-41409ffe changes it here.

  No registration step is needed for any job this watches, and there never was
  one. discover_problems() globs LAUNCH_AGENTS per watched prefix (line 185), so
  a newly installed job is covered the moment its plist lands. The installer that
  used to test for a launchd-health-register.sh and announce the watchdog absent
  is deleted; that script never existed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.kipi.launchd-health</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>__KIPI_REPO__/q-system/.q-system/scripts/launchd-health-check.py</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>9</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>21</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>30</integer></dict>
  </array>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__HOME__/.config/kipi/launchd-health.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__HOME__/.config/kipi/launchd-health.err</string>
</dict>
</plist>
